        theory: ("{D} claimed items that were never stolen.", "A real break-in and a claim made in confusion."),
        allocution: "\"The broker filled out most of that claim, and I signed it without reading closely. I moved the equipment to keep it safe, and a thief took the rest. I made a bad choice in how I handled it, and I'm sorry to the insurer.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had a prior case in this court and signed the claim after renting the unit.", "The break-in was real, and the claim form was filled out by a broker who listed every item, not just the stolen ones."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you file a false claim?", "\"I filed a claim for equipment I believed was stolen, but I had moved it myself and then lost track of where I put it.\""), .direct("Why did you move it?", "\"After the break-in, I was afraid it would be taken. I put it in a unit to keep it safe.\""), .direct("Why did you list it as stolen?", "\"I got confused. I filled out the form in a hurry, and I listed everything.\""), .direct("Did you know it was in the unit?", "\"Yes, but I didn't connect it to the claim. I wasn't thinking.\""), .direct("What did you do when the investigator found it?", "\"I told {DET.him} the truth and offered to withdraw the claim.\""), .direct("What would you tell the insurer?", "\"I'm sorry for the mistake. I'll withdraw the claim and repay anything I received.\""), .cross("You've been charged with filing a false claim before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I told the court I'd never do it again. I'm ashamed.\""), .cross("Your sworn claim says the equipment was stolen, and it was in your unit?", "\"It was in a unit I rented, and I know how that looks.\""), .cross("You listed three items that you had in storage?", "\"I did list those items as stolen, and I can't explain why I did.\""), .cross("You'll withdraw the claim?", "\"Yes, I'll withdraw the claim today and sign anything the insurer needs.\""), .cross("You'll repay any money you received?", "\"Yes, I'll repay every dollar I received from the insurer, with interest.\"")],
