        ages: 55...72,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {DL}'s case in this court in {PRIORDATE} for {PRIOR}, {D} flashed an old investigator's badge at {V}, a teen on a bicycle, and said {V} was 'under investigation' for cutting through a lot. {V} told {V.him} parents. {DL} says {D.he} only asked {V} to leave.",
        state: [E(.statement, 3, "Teen's Account", "{V} says {D} showed a badge and said {V} was under investigation."), E(.physical, 2, "Badge", "A retired badge in {D}'s car, not valid for service.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Asked to Leave", "{DL} says {D.he} only told the teen to go.")],
        role: "Teen cyclist",
        exam: [.direct("What happened to you?", "\"I was riding my bike through a parking lot when a man stopped me and showed me a badge.\""), .direct("What did the man say?", "\"That I was under investigation for cutting through the lot, and that I had to stay where I was.\""), .direct("How did you feel?", "\"Scared, because I'm only fifteen, and I thought {D.he} might call the police or take my bike.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I rode home as fast as I could and told my parents, and they called the sheriff's office.\""), .direct("What did deputies find?", "\"A retired investigator's badge in {DL}'s car, which isn't valid for any current duty.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} only asked me to leave and never said I was under investigation.\""), .cross("The man didn't touch you?", "\"No, {D.he} stood in front of my bike and blocked me.\""), .cross("The badge looked real?", "\"Yes, it looked real, with an eagle and writing on it.\""), .cross("The lot is private?", "\"Yes, the lot is private, and people had been cutting through it for weeks.\""), .cross("The man didn't follow you?", "\"No, the man didn't follow me, and he didn't touch my bike, but he blocked it.\""), .cross("You told your parents right away?", "\"Yes, I'll stop doing security work, since I can't be trusted with a badge or a lot.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used a retired badge to scare a teen.", "A retiree who asked a teen to leave."),
        allocution: "\"That badge was in my hand because it's an old one from when I worked as an investigator. I retired, and I only wanted the teen to leave the lot. It was a mistake to flash it, and I'm sorry to {V} and the family.\"",
