        truths: ("{DL} had a prior case in this court and sent the command to the tournament server on purpose.", "The tournament address was a typo of a friend's test server, and the command was sent once."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you attack the tournament's servers?", "\"I paid for a service, and I tested it, but I never meant it to hit the tournament.\""), .direct("Why did you buy it?", "\"I was curious about how it worked, and a friend challenged me to try it.\""), .direct("Did you aim it at your friend's server?", "\"I thought I did, but I must have entered the wrong address.\""), .direct("Why did the logs match the final?", "\"I ran the test during the final, and I didn't realize it would affect the same network.\""), .direct("What did you do when the organizer called?", "\"I admitted it and apologized. I offered to pay for the loss.\""), .direct("What would you tell the organizer and the sponsors?", "\"I'm sorry for the damage. I'll pay back the seventy-five hundred dollars.\""), .cross("You've been charged with attacking a network before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I assured the court that I was done making mistakes like this. I'm ashamed.\""), .cross("Your team lost earlier, and you attacked the final?", "\"It looks that way, since my team was out, and I understand why people say so.\""), .cross("You paid for an attack service?", "\"I did pay for an attack service, and that was wrong of me.\""), .cross("You'll repay the loss?", "\"Yes, I'll repay the seventy-five hundred dollars, on a plan the organizer agrees to.\""), .cross("You'll give up the account you used?", "\"Yes, I'll give up the account I used, and I'll stay off those services.\"")],
